{
  "schema": "earthsciio/scenario/v1",
  "id": "time-origin",
  "description": "A provider that counts time from a time origin (spec/esm-sources.md section 4). Each case builds the provider from the esm `entry` (named `name`) with `options`: variables, substitutions, `time_origin` (an RFC 3339 instant, or null for none) and the run `window`, in seconds from the origin (Unix seconds without one). A case with `error` fails, when the provider is built, with that code in the message. Otherwise, in seconds from the origin: `refresh_times`; `window_records` with records_per_sample 1 and 2; a PrefetchGroup of this one provider (records_per_sample 1) has the `epochs[].boundary` as its boundaries and takes `epochs[].anchor` as the anchor of each epoch; `samples[]` at model time `t` return the arrays given (file dimension order) and, for a two-record bracket, the time coordinate `time` with units `time_units`. Samples read the calendar-cadence blobs, offline.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "nei-monthly",
